XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-
Description: Kidux learning module: Mail, a child's own mailbox in Thunderbird
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is a mailbox of the child's own, in Thunderbird, with the account
 an adult gives on the adult panel: Gmail, Outlook, iCloud or any provider
 that speaks IMAP. The child has nothing to set up, and what the child
 changes in the account is put back the next time; Thunderbird's own
 policies close what a child could break, and a link in a message leads
 nowhere.
 .
 The password is given once in Thunderbird, by the adult, or in Google's or
 Microsoft's own sign-in window; Thunderbird keeps it in the child's home.
 A Google account managed with Family Link cannot sign in to Thunderbird:
 the Gmail module is for one.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
